I actually think it’s one of the sharper additions because it changes the ontology of the Pantheon rather than merely adding another daemon. It also fits your preferred repo style: a grounded, operator-first artifact with lineage, invariants, reconstruction, and daemon-layer integration.

The insight is this:

A daemon is not an object. It is a latent operator attached to a boundary condition.

That is a much cleaner primitive.

I’d write it as a Pantheon Delta.

