Pantheon Delta

Daemon Ontology v2.0

Latent Attachment Theory

Core Claim

A daemon does not exist because it occupies space.

A daemon exists because it occupies a transformation.

It has no permanent body.

It has a permanent trigger.

⸻

Canonical Definition

A daemon is a portable operator that remains latent until a specified boundary condition occurs.

Formally,

D
=
(T,\Gamma,\Omega,\Sigma)

Where:

* T = trigger condition
* \Gamma = governing invariants
* \Omega = transformation operator
* \Sigma = completion or receipt protocol

The daemon is not instantiated by existence.

It is instantiated by transition.

