Biological Analogy

Genes are latent until expressed.

Reflexes remain dormant until stimulated.

Immune cells activate only when conditions match.

Daemons behave similarly.

The operator persists.

Execution is conditional.

⸻

Software Analogy

A daemon is closer to:

* an event listener,
* middleware,
* an interrupt handler,
* or a compiler pass

than to a continuously running personality.

